Hand-forward from architect-4ae016fb, 2026-10-29, for whoever plans CQ-I06.

1. New producer row. CQ-I03 was split by SPIDR. CQ-I03a (task-c0b0775f) now delivers scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs: `<status|reconcile|cleanup> --project <abs>`, which prints one JSON line with schema moe-vm-status-v1, moe-vm-reconcile-v1 or moe-vm-cleanup-v1. I03 depends on it, and I05 (VS Code) consumes the same contract. I06 reaches it transitively through I03.

2. CI wiring is owed here. .github/workflows/ci.yml's 'Test local runner prerequisite bundles' step lists its test files explicitly. I03a could not add scripts/tests/local-runner-vm-control.test.mjs to it, because CQ-V04b1 and CQ-V04b (both unlanded) hold ci.yml. Add that file to the step in I06, after both have landed.

3. Things to check in the hardening pass:
   - ownedLedgerDir must resolve the same directory for D:/x, D:\x and /mnt/d/x;
   - cleanup deletes only ledger-owned VMs whose owner attempt is not the task's open attempt and whose lease is free;
   - cleanup needs Node 22+ for the global WebSocket. On older Node it preserves everything with DAEMON_UNREACHABLE;
   - the lease race between list_resources and the delete is a documented residual.
